<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB3-005>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB3-005" ;
  triage:title "D6 revision-distinctness test gives false assurance; doc-named tests broadly don't assert their doc line" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA1-B4 + fenix critical review I1, reviewed at 27e21224c. scripts/tests/test_render_procedure_pages.py::test_two_revisions_render_distinct_step_tables (L25-29) asserts only that whole-page text differs, true trivially via title/date scalars, and never isolates the Steps-table markup itself -- so it passes despite the byte-identical tables in BB3-001. The same doc-named-presence-not-coverage pattern recurs broadly: .just/tests/test_generate_report_index.py:62-70,65-66 (asserts field membership, not real index content); scripts/tests/test_render_procedure_pages.py:31-33 (hits the wrong missing-mermaid-flow path, not the entry-without-section path at render_procedure_pages.py:168-169), :39-47,55-56 (check=True on a clean tree detects nothing stale); source-text greps in scripts/smoke/test_run_feature_smoke.py:30-31, scripts/phase-ai/test_run_hermes_graft_live.py:26-29, scripts/smoke/test_colima_skill_report.py:69-71. Each test name promises verification the implementation does not provide." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
